  "period_note": "Year-end (31 December 2025) position from National Bank's own audited annual report \"Five Years Financial Summary\", taken from the FY2025 report (the reporting year's own document). SOLO basis including the bank's Offshore Banking Unit — the table is headed \"NBL and Its Offshore Unit\" (\"NBPLC and Its Offshore Banking Units\" from FY2025), which is National Bank's standalone presentation, not a consolidation of subsidiaries. The FY2025 report prints this table in CRORE while every other report uses MILLION. All FY2025-sourced figures have been multiplied by 10 to normalise to BDT million. The conversion is verified against the overlap: the FY2025 report's FY2024 profit after tax of -1,722.42 crore equals the FY2024 report's -17,224.21 million, and its FY2024 total assets of 57,297.82 crore equal 572,978.16 million. Total liabilities are calculated as total assets minus total shareholders' equity; the source table prints no total-liabilities line. Net interest income is calculated as interest income minus interest expenses. Classified loans are calculated as the reported NPL percentage applied to reported loans and advances, because the table gives the ratio but not the absolute figure. Note that the row this dataset maps to operating_profit is the bank's \"Profit before Tax and Provision\", so it is pre-provision operating profit; the table reports no profit-before-tax line, so profit_before_tax is not available for any year.",
